      "statusChangeNewStatus": "tracked",
      "value": "Okay, here's what's going on.\n**People cannot force themselves onto your friends list.** You *must* accept a friend request initially! This account friended a large amount of people a few years back and every person that got a friend request was given a choice to accept/deny the request. Needless to say, lots of people accepted! It was a gimmick or \"joke\" account, apparently, and was fairly well known in the Japanese community. \n**This particular user has tens of thousands of friends**, which runs into several limitations and stress cases in our friends system. (Note to self: We should implement a friend cap with some reasonable but very high number...)\nBecause of this large amount of friends, the operation to remove yourself from their friends list likely times out or errors out due to the absurd size of their friends list. We *could* manually remove you, but it's likely that anyone on that person's friend list would be in this situation if they tried to unfriend them, so we're going to keep poking at a fix.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
