      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Do you believe that pruning inactive accounts without content uploaded to them could solve this issue?\nFor this case:\nWith all of the users that this account friended, if approximately (just throwing out numbers here) 5-10% of the users on this list no longer are active, have no avatars or system_approved worlds on their account, then the chance of an active user clearing their friend list can have less headaches when it comes to cases like this.\nThere are probably other accounts on VRChat that have added users en-mass on a similar proportion.\nOther benefits to inactive account pruning:\nIt could potentially remove account clutter; lessen API calls when searching for friends. On top of that, it frees up the amount of available usernames. This could apply for both registered inactive accounts, and unregistered accounts (Steam/Meta/VIVEPORT).\nFor example, when a user signs up for a VRChat account, and wants the name \"Shadow\", it's trickier to find combinations of the name Shadow. It will open up more options for those getting into VRChat for the first time so that names can look less goofy and remain alphanumeric.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
